    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the **salutation** feature on the `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}` flow, following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` input field to `OwnerFields` (enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`).\n   - Added a read-only derived `salutation` field to `Owner`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` entity** \u2014 added a `title` column with getter/setter, mirroring the other persisted fields.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation` mapping backed by a `toSalutation(owner)` helper: returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given. The `title` itself maps automatically (enum\u2194String, verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`).\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `title` column so the value persists across create\u2192read.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `$.salutation` == `\"DR who\"`) now passes.",
