    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is clean and follows the codebase's established patterns exactly:\n\n- `toSalutation` sits alongside the existing `toAgeBand` and `toTelephoneDisplay` default methods in `OwnerMapper`, wired the same way via an `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(...)\")` on `toOwnerDto`. This is the codebase's idiom for derived read-time DTO fields, and salutation is genuinely a derivation of `title` + `lastName`, so the logic lives in the right unit. No duplication, and the mapper isn't becoming a catch-all \u2014 it's the designated home for these derivations.\n- The `title` field, column mapping, and getter/setter on `Owner` are standard JPA/bean conventions, placed consistently with sibling fields.\n- The schema change is applied uniformly across all four database dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres), which is what a maintainer would expect rather than a partial update.\n- The OpenAPI additions (`title` as a constrained input enum, `salutation` as a `readOnly` derived output) correctly distinguish the editable input from the derived output, matching how the neighboring derived fields (`initials`, `telephoneDisplay`) are documented.\n\nNothing is misplaced, duplicated, or awkward; a maintainer would find this natural.",
